            <ArticleTitle>Reactivity of the ductus arteriosus: Implications for transcatheter therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>268-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report our experience in a 13-month-old boy undergoing transcatheter coil occlusion of a patent ductus arteriosus. Constriction of the ductus arteriosus with subsequent relaxation resulted in inadvertent coil embolization. This case report and review of the literature have implications for transcatheter treatment of persistent ductus arteriosus.</AbstractText>
